  "status": "accepted-profile-names-and-scope; browser targets, source formats and corpora remain open decisions",
  "policy": [
    "These nine profile names are the accepted CE-00.1 project profiles. A profile names a scope to qualify; it is not evidence that any capability works.",
    "No support percentage is derived from type occurrence counts, registry counts or profile membership. Evidence classes stay separate.",
    "A property is required in a profile when its registry family lists that profile. CE-00.2 corpus evidence may add requirements; removing one needs an explicit reviewed decision recorded with the change.",
    "Stable in-profile gaps remain required implementation work. Runtime-unbounded needs and unsupported platforms stay visible as limitations, never as reduced denominators.",
    "Application profiles combine: a project selects one or more application profiles plus overlay and delivery profiles. ssr and reusable-package inherit the property requirements of the application profiles they deliver."
  ],
  "evidenceClasses": {
    "E1": "source-inspection: inspected upstream or PandamStyle source/documentation/data",
    "E2": "accepted-syntax-and-diagnostics: compiler admission and structured rejection fixtures",
    "E3": "emitted-transformed-css: emitted and target-transformed CSS",
    "E4": "computed-browser-behavior: computed layout/visual/state behavior in exact engines",
    "E5": "host-and-package-qualification: qualified host mode and clean archive installation"
  },
